    "body": "## Summary\n\n- `SGLDiffusionServerAPI.get_model_info` stripped `/v1` before building the request URL, but the server only registers `/models` under the `/v1` prefix (`runtime/entrypoints/openai/common_api.py`), so every call 404'd and the ComfyUI \"Load Server\" node always showed `Failed to get model info: ... 404 ...`.\n- The server's response also wraps the model card in an OpenAI-style `{\"object\": \"list\", \"data\": [...]}` envelope, so even with the URL fixed the caller got the envelope instead of the flat `task_type`/`pipeline_name`/`num_gpus` fields the docstring promises.\n- Fixed by requesting `{base_url}/models` directly and unwrapping `data[0]`, with a `RuntimeError` fallback if the response shape is ever unexpected.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Added `test/test_server_info_endpoint.py`, a CPU-only unit test mocking HTTP that checks the URL and the unwrapped response shape.\n- `py_compile` clean; full suite needs CI (no local `sglang` install in this environment).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38023209518](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38023209518)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38023209324](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38023209324)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38023209586](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38023209586)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
